PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L02U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":2,"cefr":"A1b","unit":4,"theme":"Weather and Seasons","essential_question":"How does the weather change what we do?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1","title":"It's Raining in Abha! The Present Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to form the present continuous with am/is/are + verb-ing.","Students will be able to describe what is happening now in a picture or a place.","I can say \"It's raining\" and \"The children are playing\".","I can describe what is happening now."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين المضارع المستمر باستخدام am/is/are + الفعل مع ing.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف ما يحدث الآن في صورة أو مكان.","أستطيع أن أقول It's raining وThe children are playing.","أستطيع أن أصف ما يحدث الآن."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"weather","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɛðɚ/","definition":"how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside","arabic":"الطقس","example":"The weather is lovely today.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"season","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsizən/","definition":"one of the four parts of the year","arabic":"فصل (من فصول السنة)","example":"Spring is my favorite season.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"sunny","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsʌni/","definition":"bright with lots of sunshine","arabic":"مشمس","example":"It's a sunny day at the beach.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"cloudy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈklaʊdi/","definition":"full of clouds; gray","arabic":"غائم","example":"The sky is cloudy this morning.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the present continuous for actions that are happening now, at the moment of speaking: Look! It's raining.\nForm: am / is / are + verb + -ing. I am reading. She is playing. They are swimming.\nBoth parts are needed: be + -ing. \"She reading\" is wrong – it needs is.\nI + am + verb-ing: I'm watching the rain.\nhe / she / it + is + verb-ing: It's snowing.\nyou / we / they + are + verb-ing: They're playing outside.","examples":["Look! It's snowing on the mountain.","I'm drinking hot tea.","The wind is blowing the leaves.","My brothers are building a sandcastle.","Listen! The birds are singing.","We're waiting for the bus in the rain.","Mom is closing the windows.","The sun is shining right now."],"common_errors":["✗ She reading a book now. → ✓ She is reading a book now. (Present continuous needs am/is/are.)","✗ It is rain now. → ✓ It is raining now. (Add -ing to the verb.)","✗ Look! The children play in the rain. → ✓ Look! The children are playing in the rain. (Look! = now → present continuous.)","✗ They is swimming. → ✓ They are swimming. (they → are.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم المضارع المستمر للأحداث التي تحدث الآن: It's raining (إنها تمطر الآن).\nالتركيب: am/is/are + الفعل مع ing، ولا بد من الجزأين معًا: She is reading (وليس She reading).\nكلمات مثل now وLook! وListen! تدل على المضارع المستمر."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It's Raining in Abha! The Present Continuous”. Let’s learn present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U4-LS1 | It's Raining in Abha! The Present Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Today's Weather Report”: Good morning! This is Noura with today's weather. It's raining in Abha. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Good morning! This is Noura with today's weather. It's raining in Abha.","visual":"Image GV-L02-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the present continuous for actions that are happening now, at the moment of speaking: Look! It's raining. Form: am / is / are + verb + -ing. I am reading. She is playing. They are swimming.","on_screen":"I + am + verb-ing: I'm watching the rain. • he / she / it + is + verb-ing: It's snowing. • you / we / they + are + verb-ing: They're playing outside.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Look! It's snowing on the mountain. I'm drinking hot tea. The wind is blowing the leaves.","on_screen":"Look! It's snowing on the mountain. / I'm drinking hot tea. / The wind is blowing the leaves.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “She reading a book now.” That’s not right. We say: “She is reading a book now.” Present continuous needs am/is/are.","on_screen":"✗ She reading a book now.   ✓ She is reading a book now.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"It's raining.\" Is the rain falling now? … Think! … Yes, it is – right now. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It's raining\" and \"The children are playing\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"It's raining\" and \"The children are playing\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم المضارع المستمر للأحداث التي تحدث الآن: It's raining (إنها تمطر الآن).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: She reading a book now. — الصحيح: She is reading a book now.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول It's raining وThe children are playing."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Today's Weather Report","body":"Good morning! This is Noura with today's weather.\nIt's raining in Abha. The clouds are moving over the mountains, and the wind is blowing.\nPeople are wearing jackets and carrying umbrellas.\nIn Riyadh, the sun is shining and it's very hot. Children are swimming in pools.\nIn Taif, it's cool and cloudy. Farmers are picking roses in the fields.\nHave a nice day!","word_count":63,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Look! It ___ outside.","options":["is snowing","are snowing","snows","snowing"],"answer":"is snowing","explanation":"Now / Look! / Listen! → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"now وLook! تدل على المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"I ___ my umbrella.","options":["is opening","am opening","opening","are opening"],"answer":"am opening","explanation":"I → am + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"I مع am والفعل مع ing."},{"q":"The children ___ in the garden now.","options":["is playing","playing","play","are playing"],"answer":"are playing","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."},{"q":"Listen! Someone ___ at the door.","options":["knocks","are knocking","knocking","is knocking"],"answer":"is knocking","explanation":"he / she / it → is + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"he وshe وit مع is."},{"q":"We ___ for the rain to stop.","options":["am waiting","waiting","are waiting","is waiting"],"answer":"are waiting","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."},{"q":"The sun is ___.","options":["shines","shine","shining","shined"],"answer":"shining","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing للفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write am, is or are. Word bank: are, is, 'm","items":[{"q":"The wind ______ blowing very hard.","options":[],"answer":"is","explanation":"he / she / it → is + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"he وshe وit مع is."},{"q":"I ______ wearing my warm jacket.","options":[],"answer":"'m/am","explanation":"I → am + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"I مع am والفعل مع ing."},{"q":"My cousins ______ skating on the ice.","options":[],"answer":"are","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"raining / is / in / It / Abha   ( . )","options":["raining","is","in","It","Abha"],"answer":"It is raining in Abha.","explanation":"Word order: he / she / it → is + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: he وshe وit مع is."},{"q":"are / farmers / roses / picking / The   ( . )","options":["are","farmers","roses","picking","The"],"answer":"The farmers are picking roses.","explanation":"Word order: you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: you وwe وthey مع are."},{"q":"the / am / watching / I / clouds   ( . )","options":["the","am","watching","I","clouds"],"answer":"I am watching the clouds.","explanation":"Word order: I → am + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: I مع am والفعل مع ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Look out of the window. Write what is happening.","items":[{"q":"The sky is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The sky is gray.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The sun is ___ / isn't shining.","options":[],"answer":"The sun is shining.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Some people are ___.","options":[],"answer":"Some people are walking to the mosque.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A car is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A car is stopping at the traffic light.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I am ___ right now.","options":[],"answer":"I am writing in my notebook right now.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Describe a picture.","items":[{"q":"Choose a weather picture. Write 4 sentences about what is happening.","options":[],"answer":"It is snowing. Children are making a snowman. A man is shoveling snow. A dog is running.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what your family is doing now (imagine).","options":[],"answer":"My mom is cooking. My little brother is sleeping.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Read your sentences to a partner. He guesses the picture. Write his guess.","options":[],"answer":"He thinks it is a winter picture.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing).","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"the wind"},{"label":"my brother"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"the children"},{"label":"the sun"},{"label":"you"},{"label":"the farmers"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Look! The kite ___ high in the sky.","options":["is flying","flying","are flying","flies"],"answer":"is flying","explanation":"Now / Look! / Listen! → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"now وLook! تدل على المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"I ___ hot chocolate.","options":["am drinking","drinking","are drinking","is drinking"],"answer":"am drinking","explanation":"I → am + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"I مع am والفعل مع ing."},{"q":"The boys ___ football in the rain.","options":["is playing","are playing","plays","playing"],"answer":"are playing","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."},{"q":"My sister ___ a picture of a rainbow.","options":["draws now","drawing","are drawing","is drawing"],"answer":"is drawing","explanation":"he / she / it → is + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"he وshe وit مع is."},{"q":"","options":["It is snow in the mountains.","It are snowing in the mountains.","It snowing in the mountains.","It is snowing in the mountains."],"answer":"It is snowing in the mountains.","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing للفعل."},{"q":"Listen! The rain ___ on the roof.","options":["is falling","are falling","falls","falling"],"answer":"is falling","explanation":"Now / Look! / Listen! → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"now وLook! تدل على المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["We is building a snowman.","We building a snowman.","We are build a snowman.","We are building a snowman."],"answer":"We are building a snowman.","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."},{"q":"The cat ___ in the sun.","options":["are sleeping","sleep","is sleeping","sleeping"],"answer":"is sleeping","explanation":"he / she / it → is + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"he وshe وit مع is."},{"q":"","options":["Right now, my dad are driving slowly.","Right now, my dad is driving slowly.","Right now, my dad driving slowly.","Right now, my dad drives slowly."],"answer":"Right now, my dad is driving slowly.","explanation":"Now / Look! / Listen! → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"now وLook! تدل على المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"The leaves ___ from the trees.","options":["fall now","falling","are falling","is falling"],"answer":"are falling","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Noura as a TV weather reporter in front of a map of Saudi Arabia: rain clouds over Abha, a big sun over Riyadh and clouds over Taif. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Noura as a TV weather reporter in front of a map of Saudi Arabia: rain clouds over Abha, a big sun over Riyadh and clouds over Taif"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows weather (how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing weather: how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows season (one of the four parts of the year); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing season: one of the four parts of the year"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sunny (bright with lots of sunshine); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sunny: bright with lots of sunshine"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cloudy (full of clouds; gray); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cloudy: full of clouds; gray"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W01","script":"weather. weather. The weather is lovely today.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W02","script":"season. season. Spring is my favorite season.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W03","script":"sunny. sunny. It's a sunny day at the beach.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-W04","script":"cloudy. cloudy. The sky is cloudy this morning.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-T1","script":"Good morning! This is Noura with today's weather. It's raining in Abha. The clouds are moving over the mountains, and the wind is blowing. People are wearing jackets and carrying umbrellas. In Riyadh, the sun is shining and it's very hot. Children are swimming in pools. In Taif, it's cool and cloudy. Farmers are picking roses in the fields. Have a nice day!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It's Raining in Abha! The Present Continuous”. Let’s learn present continuous affirmative (am/is/are + verb-ing) together. Listen to the start of “Today's Weather Report”: Good morning! This is Noura with today's weather. It's raining in Abha. Look at the green words. We use the present continuous for actions that are happening now, at the moment of speaking: Look! It's raining. Form: am / is / are + verb + -ing. I am reading. She is playing. They are swimming. Here are some examples. Look! It's snowing on the mountain. I'm drinking hot tea. The wind is blowing the leaves. Be careful! Some learners say: “She reading a book now.” That’s not right. We say: “She is reading a book now.” Present continuous needs am/is/are. Quick check: \"It's raining.\" Is the rain falling now? … Think! … Yes, it is – right now. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It's raining\" and \"The children are playing\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2","title":"Is It Raining? Negatives and Questions","objectives":["Students will be able to make negatives with am not, isn't and aren't + verb-ing.","Students will be able to ask yes/no and What questions in the present continuous.","I can say \"It isn't raining\".","I can ask \"Are you wearing a jacket?\" and \"What are you doing?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين النفي في المضارع المستمر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة نعم/لا وأسئلة What بالمضارع المستمر.","أستطيع أن أقول It isn't raining.","أستطيع أن أسأل Are you wearing a jacket? وWhat are you doing?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rainy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈreɪni/","definition":"with a lot of rain","arabic":"ممطر","example":"We stay inside on rainy days.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"windy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈwɪndi/","definition":"with a lot of wind","arabic":"عاصف / ذو رياح","example":"It's too windy to fly a kite.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"foggy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfɑɡi/","definition":"with thick cloud near the ground","arabic":"ضبابي","example":"Drive slowly on foggy roads.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"snowy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsnoʊi/","definition":"with a lot of snow","arabic":"مثلج","example":"The mountains are snowy in winter.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing: It isn't raining. They aren't swimming.\nYes/no questions: put am / is / are first: Is it raining? – Yes, it is. / No, it isn't.\nWhat questions: What are you doing? – I'm reading. Where is he going? – He's going to the park.","examples":["It isn't snowing today.","We aren't going to the beach – it's too windy.","I'm not wearing my jacket.","Is it raining in Taif? – No, it isn't.","Are the children playing outside? – Yes, they are.","What is Grandpa doing? – He's reading the newspaper.","Where are you going? – To the library.","Is the sun shining? – Yes, it is."],"common_errors":["✗ It not raining. → ✓ It isn't raining. (Negative needs isn't.)","✗ Do you wearing a coat? → ✓ Are you wearing a coat? (Present continuous questions use am/is/are.)","✗ What you are doing? → ✓ What are you doing? (In questions, are comes before you.)","✗ Are you playing? – Yes, I playing. → ✓ Yes, I am. (Short answer = am/is/are.)"],"arabic":"النفي: am not / isn't / aren't + الفعل مع ing: It isn't raining.\nالسؤال: نقدّم am أو is أو are: Is it raining? وما ماذا: What are you doing?\nلا نستخدم do مع المضارع المستمر: Are you wearing…? (وليس Do you wearing)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Is It Raining? Negatives and Questions”. Let’s learn present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U4-LS2 | Is It Raining? Negatives and Questions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: She is wearing a hat. She isn't wearing a hat. • I'm not feeling cold. Is she wearing a hat? – Yes, she is. / No, she isn't. • What are you doing? – I'm studying.","on_screen":"She is wearing a hat. | She isn't wearing a hat. • I'm not feeling cold. | Is she wearing a hat? – Yes, she is. / No, she isn't. • What are you doing? – I'm studying.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing: It isn't raining. They aren't swimming. Yes/no questions: put am / is / are first: Is it raining? – Yes, it is. / No, it isn't.","on_screen":"present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It isn't snowing today. We aren't going to the beach – it's too windy. I'm not wearing my jacket.","on_screen":"It isn't snowing today. / We aren't going to the beach – it's too windy. / I'm not wearing my jacket.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It not raining.” That’s not right. We say: “It isn't raining.” Negative needs isn't.","on_screen":"✗ It not raining.   ✓ It isn't raining.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"It isn't raining.\" Is the ground getting wet now? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It isn't raining\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"It isn't raining\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","النفي: am not / isn't / aren't + الفعل مع ing: It isn't raining.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It not raining. — الصحيح: It isn't raining.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول It isn't raining."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"It ___ today. The sky is clear.","options":["not raining","isn't raining","doesn't raining","aren't raining"],"answer":"isn't raining","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"___ you wearing gloves?","options":["Is","Do","Does","Are"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"What ___ your brother doing?","options":["are","does","is","do"],"answer":"is","explanation":"What/Where + am/is/are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"What ثم are ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Is it snowing? – No, it ___.","options":["aren't","doesn't","not","isn't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it is. / No, they aren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"We ___ playing outside. It's too hot.","options":["aren't","not","don't","isn't"],"answer":"aren't","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"Are your friends coming? – Yes, they ___.","options":["do","is","are","come"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it is. / No, they aren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make the sentences negative.","items":[{"q":"The wind is blowing.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"The wind isn't blowing.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"I am feeling cold.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"I'm not feeling cold.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"The boys are flying kites.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"The boys aren't flying kites.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions.","items":[{"q":"It is getting dark.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Is it getting dark?","explanation":"Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"They are carrying umbrellas.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Are they carrying umbrellas?","explanation":"Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"You are doing your homework. (What)","options":[],"answer":"What are you doing?","explanation":"What/Where + am/is/are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"What ثم are ثم الفاعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about right now.","items":[{"q":"Is it raining where you are?","options":[],"answer":"No, it isn't. It's sunny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What are you wearing today?","options":[],"answer":"I'm wearing a white thobe.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Are you sitting next to the window?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I am.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What is your teacher doing?","options":[],"answer":"He is writing on the board.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Are your classmates talking?","options":[],"answer":"No, they aren't. They're working.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Video call role-play.","items":[{"q":"Write a 6-line video call with a cousin in another city about the weather and what you are doing.","options":[],"answer":"A: Is it raining in Abha? B: Yes, it is. A: What are you doing? B: I'm reading. A: It's sunny here. We're going to the park.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what is NOT happening in your class now.","options":[],"answer":"We aren't eating. The teacher isn't sitting.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner 2 \"What are you doing…?\" questions and write his answers.","options":[],"answer":"What are you doing after school? – He's playing football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"it / rain / now / –"},{"cue":"the children / play / outside / ?"},{"cue":"the sun / shine / +"},{"cue":"you / wear / a coat / ?"},{"cue":"we / swim / today / –"},{"cue":"the wind / blow / +"},{"cue":"Dad / drive / in the fog / ?"},{"cue":"the birds / sing / +"},{"cue":"I / feel / cold / –"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The sun ___ today. It's cloudy.","options":["isn't shining","aren't shine","not shining","doesn't shining"],"answer":"isn't shining","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"___ it raining in Jeddah?","options":["Does","Is","Do","Are"],"answer":"Is","explanation":"Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"What ___ you doing? – I'm making soup.","options":["are","does","do","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"What/Where + am/is/are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"What ثم are ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Are you listening? – Yes, I ___.","options":["listen","is","am","do"],"answer":"am","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it is. / No, they aren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"","options":["I not wearing a coat.","I don't wearing a coat.","I amn't wearing a coat.","I'm not wearing a coat."],"answer":"I'm not wearing a coat.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"","options":["Do the birds singing?","Is the birds singing?","Are the birds singing?","The birds are singing?"],"answer":"Are the birds singing?","explanation":"Don't use do with the present continuous.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم do مع المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Where is Dad going?","Where Dad is going?","Where is Dad go?","Where does Dad going?"],"answer":"Where is Dad going?","explanation":"What/Where + am/is/are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"What ثم are ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Is your brother sleeping? – No, he ___.","options":["aren't","isn't","not","doesn't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it is. / No, they aren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"","options":["We not swimming today.","We don't swimming today.","We isn't swimming today.","We aren't swimming today."],"answer":"We aren't swimming today.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"___ the children making a snowman?","options":["Do","Are","Does","Is"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Two friends talking on video call: Adam in a rainy window with an umbrella and Omar in a sunny garden, each asking what the other is doing. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two friends talking on video call: Adam in a rainy window with an umbrella and Omar in a sunny garden, each asking what the other is doing"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?): a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Weather and Seasons”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rainy (with a lot of rain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rainy: with a lot of rain"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows windy (with a lot of wind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing windy: with a lot of wind"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows foggy (with thick cloud near the ground); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing foggy: with thick cloud near the ground"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows snowy (with a lot of snow); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing snowy: with a lot of snow"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W01","script":"rainy. rainy. We stay inside on rainy days.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W02","script":"windy. windy. It's too windy to fly a kite.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W03","script":"foggy. foggy. Drive slowly on foggy roads.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-W04","script":"snowy. snowy. The mountains are snowy in winter.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Is It Raining? Negatives and Questions”. Let’s learn present continuous negative and questions (isn't/aren't; Is it…? Are you…? What are you doing?) together. Remember these patterns: She is wearing a hat. She isn't wearing a hat. • I'm not feeling cold. Is she wearing a hat? – Yes, she is. / No, she isn't. • What are you doing? – I'm studying. Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing: It isn't raining. They aren't swimming. Yes/no questions: put am / is / are first: Is it raining? – Yes, it is. / No, it isn't. Here are some examples. It isn't snowing today. We aren't going to the beach – it's too windy. I'm not wearing my jacket. Be careful! Some learners say: “It not raining.” That’s not right. We say: “It isn't raining.” Negative needs isn't. Quick check: \"It isn't raining.\" Is the ground getting wet now? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"It isn't raining\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3","title":"Sun, Sunny! Weather Words with -y","objectives":["Students will be able to make weather adjectives by adding -y to nouns.","Students will be able to choose clothes and things for different weather.","I can say \"rain → rainy\" and \"wind → windy\".","I can say what to wear in different weather."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين صفات الطقس بإضافة y إلى الأسماء.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار الملابس والأدوات المناسبة للطقس.","أستطيع أن أقول rain → rainy وwind → windy.","أستطيع أن أقول ماذا نرتدي في الطقس المختلف."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"hot","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/hɑt/","definition":"very warm","arabic":"حار","example":"Riyadh is very hot in August.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"cold","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/koʊld/","definition":"not warm; low temperature","arabic":"بارد","example":"The water in the pool is cold.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"umbrella","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əmˈbrɛlə/","definition":"a thing you hold over your head in the rain","arabic":"مظلة","example":"Take an umbrella – it's raining!","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"jacket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdʒækət/","definition":"a short coat","arabic":"سترة / جاكيت","example":"Wear your jacket in the evening.","image_id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Many weather adjectives are made by adding -y to a noun: sun → sunny, cloud → cloudy, rain → rainy, wind → windy, snow → snowy, storm → stormy.\nSpelling: one short vowel + one consonant → double it: sun → sunny, fog → foggy.\nTemperature words go from very cold to very hot: freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot. We say It's + adjective: It's windy.\nCollocations/phrases: sun → sunny • cloud → cloudy • rain → rainy • wind → windy • snow → snowy • storm → stormy • fog → foggy | freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot | rainy → umbrella, raincoat • cold → jacket, scarf • sunny → sunglasses, hat","examples":["It's sunny, so wear your sunglasses.","The mountains are snowy in January.","It's foggy on the road to Al-Hada.","Take an umbrella; it's rainy.","Put on your jacket. It's cold outside.","Spring in Taif is warm and green.","A stormy night is noisy and dark.","Which season do you like best?"],"common_errors":["✗ It's sun today. → ✓ It's sunny today. (After It's, use the adjective (sun → sunny).)","✗ It's very fogy. → ✓ It's very foggy. (Double the g: fog → foggy.)","✗ The weather is very hotly. → ✓ The weather is very hot. (hot is the adjective.)","✗ I wear an umbrella. → ✓ I carry / take an umbrella. (We wear clothes; we carry an umbrella.)"],"arabic":"نضيف y إلى اسم الطقس لنحصل على صفة: sun → sunny (مشمس)، rain → rainy (ممطر).\nإذا كانت الكلمة حرفًا متحركًا قصيرًا وحرفًا ساكنًا نضاعف الحرف: sun → sunny وfog → foggy.\nنقول It's sunny (الجو مشمس) وليس It's sun.\nنقول carry an umbrella (نحمل مظلة) وليس wear."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Sun, Sunny! Weather Words with -y”. Let’s learn weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U4-LS3 | Sun, Sunny! Weather Words with -y","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. hot: very warm. cold: not warm; low temperature. umbrella: a thing you hold over your head in the rain.","on_screen":"hot | cold | umbrella","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Many weather adjectives are made by adding -y to a noun: sun → sunny, cloud → cloudy, rain → rainy, wind → windy, snow → snowy, storm → stormy. Spelling: one short vowel + one consonant → double it: sun → sunny, fog → foggy.","on_screen":"weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It's sunny, so wear your sunglasses. The mountains are snowy in January. It's foggy on the road to Al-Hada.","on_screen":"It's sunny, so wear your sunglasses. / The mountains are snowy in January. / It's foggy on the road to Al-Hada.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It's sun today.” That’s not right. We say: “It's sunny today.” After It's, use the adjective (sun → sunny).","on_screen":"✗ It's sun today.   ✓ It's sunny today.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which word is the adjective: \"wind\" or \"windy\"? … Think! … *windy* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"rain → rainy\" and \"wind → windy\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"rain → rainy\" and \"wind → windy\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نضيف y إلى اسم الطقس لنحصل على صفة: sun → sunny (مشمس)، rain → rainy (ممطر).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It's sun today. — الصحيح: It's sunny today.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول rain → rainy وwind → windy."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"There are many clouds. It's ___.","options":["cloudy","cloud","clouds","cloudly"],"answer":"cloudy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"The wind is very strong. It's ___.","options":["winds","windy","windly","wind"],"answer":"windy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"It's ___. I can't see the road!","options":["fogs","fog","fogy","foggy"],"answer":"foggy","explanation":"Short vowel + one consonant → double it (sunny, foggy).","explanation_ar":"ضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"It's 40°C. It's very ___.","options":["hot","freezing","cold","cool"],"answer":"hot","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"It's raining. Take your ___.","options":["swimsuit","sunglasses","umbrella","sandals"],"answer":"umbrella","explanation":"wear clothes; carry/take an umbrella.","explanation_ar":"نرتدي الملابس ونحمل المظلة."},{"q":"Snow is falling. It's a ___ day.","options":["snows","snowy","snow","snowly"],"answer":"snowy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the adjective.","items":[{"q":"storm  (adjective)","options":[],"answer":"stormy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"sun  (adjective)","options":[],"answer":"sunny","explanation":"Short vowel + one consonant → double it (sunny, foggy).","explanation_ar":"ضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"rain  (adjective)","options":[],"answer":"rainy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with a temperature word: cold, cool, warm, hot. Word bank: cold, cool, hot","items":[{"q":"Put on a scarf. It's very ______ today.","options":[],"answer":"cold","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"The evening in Taif is ______, not hot.","options":[],"answer":"cool","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"Summer in Riyadh is very ______.","options":[],"answer":"hot","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about the weather where you live.","items":[{"q":"Today it is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Today it is sunny and hot.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In winter, my city is ___.","options":[],"answer":"In winter, my city is cool and rainy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"On a rainy day, I take ___.","options":[],"answer":"On a rainy day, I take an umbrella.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"On a cold day, I wear ___.","options":[],"answer":"On a cold day, I wear a jacket and a scarf.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite season is ___ because ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite season is spring because it is warm.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a weather chart.","items":[{"q":"Draw a chart for 5 days with a weather picture and a word for each day.","options":[],"answer":"Sunday – sunny; Monday – cloudy; Tuesday – rainy; Wednesday – windy; Thursday – sunny","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your chart.","options":[],"answer":"On Monday, it is cloudy. On Tuesday, it is rainy. On Wednesday, it is windy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write what to wear for 2 days on your chart.","options":[],"answer":"On Tuesday, wear a raincoat. On Thursday, wear a hat.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"weather","match":"how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside","arabic":"الطقس"},{"word":"season","match":"one of the four parts of the year","arabic":"فصل (من فصول السنة)"},{"word":"sunny","match":"bright with lots of sunshine","arabic":"مشمس"},{"word":"cloudy","match":"full of clouds; gray","arabic":"غائم"},{"word":"rainy","match":"with a lot of rain","arabic":"ممطر"},{"word":"windy","match":"with a lot of wind","arabic":"عاصف / ذو رياح"},{"word":"foggy","match":"with thick cloud near the ground","arabic":"ضبابي"},{"word":"snowy","match":"with a lot of snow","arabic":"مثلج"},{"word":"hot","match":"very warm","arabic":"حار"},{"word":"cold","match":"not warm; low temperature","arabic":"بارد"},{"word":"umbrella","match":"a thing you hold over your head in the rain","arabic":"مظلة"},{"word":"jacket","match":"a short coat","arabic":"سترة / جاكيت"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"storm → ___","options":["storms","stormy","stormmy","stormly"],"answer":"stormy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"sun → ___","options":["suny","sunny","sunly","suns"],"answer":"sunny","explanation":"Short vowel + one consonant → double it (sunny, foggy).","explanation_ar":"ضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"It's 2°C. It's ___.","options":["freezing","warm","hot","sunny"],"answer":"freezing","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"It's very bright. Wear your ___.","options":["raincoat","gloves","sunglasses","boots"],"answer":"sunglasses","explanation":"wear clothes; carry/take an umbrella.","explanation_ar":"نرتدي الملابس ونحمل المظلة."},{"q":"","options":["It's windly today.","It's windy today.","It's wind today.","It's winds today."],"answer":"It's windy today.","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"Which is warmer?","options":["cool","freezing","warm","cold"],"answer":"warm","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"","options":["I carry a umbrella on rainy days.","I carry an umbrella on rain days.","I carry an umbrella on rainy days.","I wear an umbrella on rainy days."],"answer":"I carry an umbrella on rainy days.","explanation":"wear clothes; carry/take an umbrella.","explanation_ar":"نرتدي الملابس ونحمل المظلة."},{"q":"Spring, summer, fall and winter are the four ___.","options":["seasons","weathers","months","days"],"answer":"seasons","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"It's ___ in the mountains. Everything is white.","options":["hot","foggy","sunny","snowy"],"answer":"snowy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"fog → ___","options":["fogly","fogy","foggly","foggy"],"answer":"foggy","explanation":"Short vowel + one consonant → double it (sunny, foggy).","explanation_ar":"ضاعف الحرف الأخير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"Four weather panels in a row – sunny beach, rainy street with umbrellas, windy park with kites and snowy mountain – each with a child in matching clothes. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Four weather panels in a row – sunny beach, rainy street with umbrellas, windy park with kites and snowy mountain – each with a child in matching clothes"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hot (very warm); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hot: very warm"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cold (not warm; low temperature); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cold: not warm; low temperature"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows umbrella (a thing you hold over your head in the rain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing umbrella: a thing you hold over your head in the rain"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows jacket (a short coat); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing jacket: a short coat"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W01","script":"hot. hot. Riyadh is very hot in August.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W02","script":"cold. cold. The water in the pool is cold.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W03","script":"umbrella. umbrella. Take an umbrella – it's raining!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-W04","script":"jacket. jacket. Wear your jacket in the evening.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Sun, Sunny! Weather Words with -y”. Let’s learn weather nouns and adjectives (sun → sunny); temperature words and clothes for weather together. Meet some new words. hot: very warm. cold: not warm; low temperature. umbrella: a thing you hold over your head in the rain. Many weather adjectives are made by adding -y to a noun: sun → sunny, cloud → cloudy, rain → rainy, wind → windy, snow → snowy, storm → stormy. Spelling: one short vowel + one consonant → double it: sun → sunny, fog → foggy. Here are some examples. It's sunny, so wear your sunglasses. The mountains are snowy in January. It's foggy on the road to Al-Hada. Be careful! Some learners say: “It's sun today.” That’s not right. We say: “It's sunny today.” After It's, use the adjective (sun → sunny). Quick check: Which word is the adjective: \"wind\" or \"windy\"? … Think! … *windy* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"rain → rainy\" and \"wind → windy\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4","title":"Swimming, Making, Playing: Spelling with -ing","objectives":["Students will be able to spell -ing forms (playing, making, swimming, lying).","Students will be able to correct -ing spelling mistakes in sentences.","I can spell \"making\" and \"swimming\".","I can fix -ing spelling mistakes."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تهجئة صيغ ing بشكل صحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيح أخطاء تهجئة ing في الجمل.","أستطيع أن أتهجّى making وswimming.","أستطيع أن أصحح أخطاء تهجئة ing."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"weather","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɛðɚ/","definition":"how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside","arabic":"الطقس","example":"The weather is lovely today.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"season","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsizən/","definition":"one of the four parts of the year","arabic":"فصل (من فصول السنة)","example":"Spring is my favorite season.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sunny","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsʌni/","definition":"bright with lots of sunshine","arabic":"مشمس","example":"It's a sunny day at the beach.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cloudy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈklaʊdi/","definition":"full of clouds; gray","arabic":"غائم","example":"The sky is cloudy this morning.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rainy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈreɪni/","definition":"with a lot of rain","arabic":"ممطر","example":"We stay inside on rainy days.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"windy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈwɪndi/","definition":"with a lot of wind","arabic":"عاصف / ذو رياح","example":"It's too windy to fly a kite.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Most verbs just add -ing: play → playing, rain → raining.\nVerbs ending in silent -e: drop the e and add -ing: make → making, ride → riding.\nShort verbs with one vowel + one consonant (CVC): double the last letter: swim → swimming, run → running, sit → sitting. Verbs ending in -ie: change to y: lie → lying, tie → tying.\n+ ing: reading, snowing, blowing\nsilent e → drop e + ing: writing, smiling, shining\none vowel + one consonant → double + ing: running, getting, stopping\nie → y + ing: lying, dying, tying","examples":["The sun is shining.","We're swimming in the sea.","Dad is writing an email.","My sister is sitting by the window.","The baby is lying on the bed.","The cars are stopping at the light.","Rakan is riding his bike.","The kids are running in the rain."],"common_errors":["✗ makeing → ✓ making (Drop the silent e.)","✗ swiming → ✓ swimming (Double the m.)","✗ lieing → ✓ lying (ie → y.)","✗ rainning → ✓ raining (Two vowels (ai) → don't double.)"],"arabic":"معظم الأفعال نضيف لها ing مباشرة: playing.\nالفعل المنتهي بـ e صامتة نحذف e: make → making.\nالفعل القصير (متحرك واحد + ساكن واحد) نضاعف آخره: swim → swimming.\nie تتحول إلى y: lie → lying."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Swimming, Making, Playing: Spelling with -ing”. Let’s learn spelling rules for verb + -ing together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U4-LS4 | Swimming, Making, Playing: Spelling with -ing","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Most verbs just add -ing: play → playing, rain → raining.","on_screen":"spelling rules for verb + -ing","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Most verbs just add -ing: play → playing, rain → raining. Verbs ending in silent -e: drop the e and add -ing: make → making, ride → riding.","on_screen":"+ ing: reading, snowing, blowing • silent e → drop e + ing: writing, smiling, shining • one vowel + one consonant → double + ing: running, getting, stopping","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The sun is shining. We're swimming in the sea. Dad is writing an email.","on_screen":"The sun is shining. / We're swimming in the sea. / Dad is writing an email.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “makeing.” That’s not right. We say: “making.” Drop the silent e.","on_screen":"✗ makeing   ✓ making","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Why do we double the m in \"swimming\"? … Think! … swim = one vowel + one consonant. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"making\" and \"swimming\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can spell \"making\" and \"swimming\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: spelling rules for verb + -ing.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","معظم الأفعال نضيف لها ing مباشرة: playing.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: makeing — الصحيح: making","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتهجّى making وswimming."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Weather Blog – Saturday (editing passage)","body":"Today it is snoing in Tabuk! Children are makeing snowmen. My uncle is driveing slowly. The cars are stoping at the corner. I'm siting by the fire and drinkking tea.","word_count":30,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct spelling.","items":[{"q":"run → ___","options":["runnning","runing","runeing","running"],"answer":"running","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"make → ___","options":["makin","makking","makeing","making"],"answer":"making","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"tie → ___","options":["tyeing","tying","tiing","tieing"],"answer":"tying","explanation":"ie → y + ing.","explanation_ar":"ie تتحول إلى y."},{"q":"snow → ___","options":["snowing","snowng","snowwing","snoing"],"answer":"snowing","explanation":"Two vowels or w/x/y at the end → don't double.","explanation_ar":"لا نضاعف بعد حرفين متحركين."},{"q":"write → ___","options":["writng","writting","writing","writeing"],"answer":"writing","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"sit → ___","options":["siteing","sitting","sittting","siting"],"answer":"sitting","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the spelling mistake.","items":[{"q":"The children are swiming in the lake.","options":[],"answer":"The children are swimming in the lake.","explanation":"swiming → swimming. One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: swiming → swimming. نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"Mom is bakeing bread.","options":[],"answer":"Mom is baking bread.","explanation":"bakeing → baking. Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: bakeing → baking. نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"The cat is lieing in the sun.","options":[],"answer":"The cat is lying in the sun.","explanation":"lieing → lying. ie → y + ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: lieing → lying. ie تتحول إلى y."},{"q":"It is rainning in Abha.","options":[],"answer":"It is raining in Abha.","explanation":"rainning → raining. Two vowels or w/x/y at the end → don't double.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: rainning → raining. لا نضاعف بعد حرفين متحركين."},{"q":"We are geting ready for school.","options":[],"answer":"We are getting ready for school.","explanation":"geting → getting. One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: geting → getting. نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"The teacher is smileing.","options":[],"answer":"The teacher is smiling.","explanation":"smileing → smiling. Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: smileing → smiling. نحذف e الصامتة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the weather blog.","items":[{"q":"Today it is snoing in Tabuk!","options":[],"answer":"Today it is snowing in Tabuk!","explanation":"snoing → snowing. Most verbs: add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: snoing → snowing. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ing."},{"q":"Children are makeing snowmen.","options":[],"answer":"Children are making snowmen.","explanation":"makeing → making. Most verbs: add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: makeing → making. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ing."},{"q":"My uncle is driveing slowly.","options":[],"answer":"My uncle is driving slowly.","explanation":"driveing → driving. Most verbs: add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: driveing → driving. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ing."},{"q":"The cars are stoping at the corner.","options":[],"answer":"The cars are stopping at the corner.","explanation":"stoping → stopping. Most verbs: add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: stoping → stopping. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ing."},{"q":"I'm siting by the fire and drinking tea.","options":[],"answer":"I'm sitting by the fire and drinking tea.","explanation":"siting → sitting. Most verbs: add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: siting → sitting. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ing."},{"q":"I'm sitting by the fire and drinkking tea.","options":[],"answer":"I'm sitting by the fire and drinking tea.","explanation":"drinkking → drinking. Most verbs: add -ing.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: drinkking → drinking. معظم الأفعال: نضيف ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write -ing sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 -ing words, one for each rule.","options":[],"answer":"playing, making, running, lying","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules for verb + -ing correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a rainy day with -ing verbs.","options":[],"answer":"The rain is falling. People are running. A man is opening his umbrella.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules for verb + -ing correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check your partner's -ing spelling. Write one correction.","options":[],"answer":"\"runing\" → \"running\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses spelling rules for verb + -ing correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"raining","clue":""},{"word":"snowing","clue":""},{"word":"shining","clue":""},{"word":"swimming","clue":""},{"word":"running","clue":""},{"word":"making","clue":""},{"word":"sitting","clue":""},{"word":"lying","clue":""},{"word":"writing","clue":""},{"word":"stopping","clue":""},{"word":"weather","clue":"how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside"},{"word":"season","clue":"one of the four parts of the year"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"swim → ___","options":["swimeing","swimming","swimmming","swiming"],"answer":"swimming","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"ride → ___","options":["ridding","rideing","riding","ridng"],"answer":"riding","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"lie → ___","options":["lyeing","lieing","lying","liing"],"answer":"lying","explanation":"ie → y + ing.","explanation_ar":"ie تتحول إلى y."},{"q":"play → ___","options":["playing","plaiying","plaing","playying"],"answer":"playing","explanation":"Two vowels or w/x/y at the end → don't double.","explanation_ar":"لا نضاعف بعد حرفين متحركين."},{"q":"","options":["The sun is shining.","The sun is shinng.","The sun is shinning.","The sun is shineing."],"answer":"The sun is shining.","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"stop → ___","options":["stopiing","stoping","stopeing","stopping"],"answer":"stopping","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"","options":["My brother is fixxing his bike.","My brother is fixing his bike.","My brother is fiksing his bike.","My brother is fixeing his bike."],"answer":"My brother is fixing his bike.","explanation":"Two vowels or w/x/y at the end → don't double.","explanation_ar":"لا نضاعف بعد حرفين متحركين."},{"q":"Which -ing word is spelled correctly?","options":["comng","coming","comeing","comming"],"answer":"coming","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"","options":["We are sitting in the shade.","We are siting in the shade.","We are siteing in the shade.","We are sittting in the shade."],"answer":"We are sitting in the shade.","explanation":"One vowel + one consonant → double the last letter.","explanation_ar":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"rain → ___","options":["rainning","raineing","rainin","raining"],"answer":"raining","explanation":"Two vowels or w/x/y at the end → don't double.","explanation_ar":"لا نضاعف بعد حرفين متحركين."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Weather and Seasons” that shows spelling rules for verb + -ing in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Weather and Seasons” that shows spelling rules for verb + -ing in action"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Swimming, Making, Playing: Spelling with -ing”. Let’s learn spelling rules for verb + -ing together. Most verbs just add -ing: play → playing, rain → raining. Most verbs just add -ing: play → playing, rain → raining. Verbs ending in silent -e: drop the e and add -ing: make → making, ride → riding. Here are some examples. The sun is shining. We're swimming in the sea. Dad is writing an email. Be careful! Some learners say: “makeing.” That’s not right. We say: “making.” Drop the silent e. Quick check: Why do we double the m in \"swimming\"? … Think! … swim = one vowel + one consonant. Great job! Now you can say: I can spell \"making\" and \"swimming\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5","title":"Our Weather Report: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to give a weather report describing what is happening now.","Students will be able to write a weather report with correct present continuous forms and -ing spelling.","I can present a weather report.","I can write about the weather and what people are doing."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم نشرة جوية تصف ما يحدث الآن.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة نشرة جوية بصيغ المضارع المستمر وتهجئة ing صحيحة.","أستطيع أن أقدّم نشرة جوية.","أستطيع أن أكتب عن الطقس وما يفعله الناس."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"weather","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɛðɚ/","definition":"how hot, cold, wet or windy it is outside","arabic":"الطقس","example":"The weather is lovely today.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"season","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsizən/","definition":"one of the four parts of the year","arabic":"فصل (من فصول السنة)","example":"Spring is my favorite season.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sunny","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsʌni/","definition":"bright with lots of sunshine","arabic":"مشمس","example":"It's a sunny day at the beach.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cloudy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈklaʊdi/","definition":"full of clouds; gray","arabic":"غائم","example":"The sky is cloudy this morning.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rainy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈreɪni/","definition":"with a lot of rain","arabic":"ممطر","example":"We stay inside on rainy days.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"windy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈwɪndi/","definition":"with a lot of wind","arabic":"عاصف / ذو رياح","example":"It's too windy to fly a kite.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"foggy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfɑɡi/","definition":"with thick cloud near the ground","arabic":"ضبابي","example":"Drive slowly on foggy roads.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"snowy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsnoʊi/","definition":"with a lot of snow","arabic":"مثلج","example":"The mountains are snowy in winter.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hot","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/hɑt/","definition":"very warm","arabic":"حار","example":"Riyadh is very hot in August.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cold","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/koʊld/","definition":"not warm; low temperature","arabic":"بارد","example":"The water in the pool is cold.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"umbrella","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əmˈbrɛlə/","definition":"a thing you hold over your head in the rain","arabic":"مظلة","example":"Take an umbrella – it's raining!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"jacket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdʒækət/","definition":"a short coat","arabic":"سترة / جاكيت","example":"Wear your jacket in the evening.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the present continuous (positive, negative, questions), weather words and -ing spelling.\nA weather report gives the place, the weather now and what people are doing. It often ends with advice (Take…, Wear…).\n✔ am/is/are + verb-ing for now\n✔ isn't / aren't for negatives; Is…? Are…? What…? for questions\n✔ weather adjectives: sunny, rainy, windy…\n✔ correct -ing spelling","examples":["It's raining heavily in Abha.","People are carrying umbrellas.","It isn't snowing in Riyadh.","Is the wind blowing in Dammam? – Yes, it is.","Fishermen aren't sailing today. It's stormy.","What are people doing in the park? – They're having picnics.","Take sunglasses – it's very sunny.","Families are sitting by the fire."],"common_errors":["✗ In Tabuk is snowing. → ✓ In Tabuk, it is snowing. (English needs a subject: it.)","✗ People is walking by the sea. → ✓ People are walking by the sea. (people is plural → are.)","✗ It's very wind. → ✓ It's very windy. (Use the adjective.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المضارع المستمر بالإثبات والنفي والسؤال، وكلمات الطقس، وتهجئة ing.\nفي الإنجليزية نحتاج الفاعل it مع الطقس: It is snowing (وليس Is snowing).\nكلمة people جمع، لذلك نقول people are."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Weather Report: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U4-LS5 | Our Weather Report: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Class weather show: in pairs, one student is the reporter in a city and one is in the studio. The studio asks \"What's the weather like? What are people doing?\" The reporter answers with the present continuous.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the present continuous (positive, negative, questions), weather words and -ing spelling. A weather report gives the place, the weather now and what people are doing. It often ends with advice (Take…, Wear…).","on_screen":"✔ am/is/are + verb-ing for now • ✔ isn't / aren't for negatives; Is…? Are…? What…? for questions • ✔ weather adjectives: sunny, rainy, windy…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It's raining heavily in Abha. People are carrying umbrellas. It isn't snowing in Riyadh.","on_screen":"It's raining heavily in Abha. / People are carrying umbrellas. / It isn't snowing in Riyadh.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “In Tabuk is snowing.” That’s not right. We say: “In Tabuk, it is snowing.” English needs a subject: it.","on_screen":"✗ In Tabuk is snowing.   ✓ In Tabuk, it is snowing.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “People is walking by the sea.”? … Think! … It should be “People are walking by the sea.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present a weather report.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can present a weather report.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المضارع المستمر بالإثبات والنفي والسؤال، وكلمات الطقس، وتهجئة ing.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: In Tabuk is snowing. — الصحيح: In Tabuk, it is snowing.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم نشرة جوية."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Weekend Weather – Yusuf","body":"Hello, everyone! Here is the weekend weather.\nIn Tabuk, it's snowing! Children are playing in the snow, and families are drinking hot tea.\nIn Jeddah, it isn't cold. The sun is shining, and people are walking by the sea.\nAre you going to Tabuk? Take a warm jacket and gloves!\nEnjoy your weekend!","word_count":53,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's report. True or False?","items":[{"q":"It's snowing in Tabuk.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Weekend Weather – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Children in Tabuk are swimming.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Weekend Weather – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It's cold in Jeddah.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Weekend Weather – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"People in Jeddah are walking by the sea.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Weekend Weather – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf says to take a warm jacket to Tabuk.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Weekend Weather – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The sun isn't shining in Jeddah.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Weekend Weather – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"In Tabuk, families ___ hot tea.","options":["are drinking","drinking","is drinking","drink now"],"answer":"are drinking","explanation":"am/is/are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"In Jeddah, ___ isn't cold.","options":["they","there","is","it"],"answer":"it","explanation":"Weather sentences need it: It's raining.","explanation_ar":"جمل الطقس تحتاج it."},{"q":"There's a lot of wind. It's ___.","options":["winds","windly","windy","wind"],"answer":"windy","explanation":"Choose the right weather word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطقس الصحيحة."},{"q":"The children are ___ in the snow. (run)","options":["runs","runing","runeing","running"],"answer":"running","explanation":"Check the -ing spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة ing."},{"q":"___ people walking by the sea? – Yes, they are.","options":["Is","Are","Do","Does"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Questions: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بالمضارع المستمر."},{"q":"People ___ by the sea.","options":["is walking","are walking","walking","walks now"],"answer":"are walking","explanation":"am/is/are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"المضارع المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Weather show. Write your questions and answers.","items":[{"q":"Studio asks: \"What's the weather like in ___?\"","options":[],"answer":"What's the weather like in Abha?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Reporter answers: \"It's ___.\"","options":[],"answer":"It's cloudy and cool.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Studio asks: \"What are people doing?\"","options":[],"answer":"What are people doing?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Reporter answers with 2 actions.","options":[],"answer":"They're walking in the park. Some are taking photos.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Reporter gives advice: \"Take…\" or \"Wear…\".","options":[],"answer":"Wear a jacket in the evening.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your weather report.","items":[{"q":"Plan: two places, the weather and what people are doing.","options":[],"answer":"Taif – windy; people flying kites. Riyadh – hot; people staying inside.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your report in 5–6 sentences with one negative and one question.","options":[],"answer":"Hello! In Taif, it's windy. Children are flying kites. In Riyadh, it's very hot. People aren't walking outside. Are you going out? Take water!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: am/is/are? -ing spelling? weather adjectives? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"fliing\" to \"flying\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"weather","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"season","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sunny","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cloudy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"rainy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"windy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"foggy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"snowy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hot","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cold","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"umbrella","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"jacket","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Look! The children ___ a snowman.","options":["are making","is making","make now","making"],"answer":"are making","explanation":"am/is/are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"___ is foggy on the mountain road.","options":["There","Is","This","It"],"answer":"It","explanation":"Weather sentences need it: It's raining.","explanation_ar":"جمل الطقس تحتاج it."},{"q":"The sky is gray and full of clouds. It's ___.","options":["snowy","sunny","cloudy","foggy"],"answer":"cloudy","explanation":"Choose the right weather word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطقس الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["People are lieing on the beach.","People is lying on the beach.","People are lying on the beach.","People are liing on the beach."],"answer":"People are lying on the beach.","explanation":"Check the -ing spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة ing."},{"q":"","options":["The wind is blowing hard?","Is the wind blowing hard?","Does the wind blowing hard?","Is the wind blow hard?"],"answer":"Is the wind blowing hard?","explanation":"Questions: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بالمضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["It not raining in Riyadh today.","It isn't raining in Riyadh today.","Isn't raining in Riyadh today.","It doesn't raining in Riyadh today."],"answer":"It isn't raining in Riyadh today.","explanation":"am/is/are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"What ___ the fishermen doing?","options":["are","do","does","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Questions: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بالمضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["It very hot, so take water.","It's very hotly, so take water.","Is very hot, so take water.","It's very hot, so take water."],"answer":"It's very hot, so take water.","explanation":"Weather sentences need it: It's raining.","explanation_ar":"جمل الطقس تحتاج it."},{"q":"The boys are ___ kites in the wind. (fly)","options":["flyeing","flys","flying","fliing"],"answer":"flying","explanation":"Check the -ing spelling.","explanation_ar":"تحقق من تهجئة ing."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a weather report:","options":["In abha, it's raining and people are wearing umbrellas.","In Abha, it's raining and people are carrying umbrellas.","In Abha, it rains now and people is carrying umbrellas.","In Abha, is raining and people carrying umbrellas."],"answer":"In Abha, it's raining and people are carrying umbrellas.","explanation":"am/is/are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"المضارع المستمر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Yusuf and Lina presenting a class weather report in front of a hand-drawn map with sun and cloud stickers; classmates holding a toy microphone. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Yusuf and Lina presenting a class weather report in front of a hand-drawn map with sun and cloud stickers; classmates holding a toy microphone"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Weather and Seasons”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Weather and Seasons”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L02-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS5-T1","script":"Hello, everyone! Here is the weekend weather. In Tabuk, it's snowing! Children are playing in the snow, and families are drinking hot tea. In Jeddah, it isn't cold. The sun is shining, and people are walking by the sea. Are you going to Tabuk? Take a warm jacket and gloves! Enjoy your weekend!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Weather Report: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present continuous (all forms), weather words and -ing spelling (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Class weather show: in pairs, one student is the reporter in a city and one is in the studio. The studio asks \"What's the weather like? What are people doing?\" The reporter answers with the present continuous. Today you use all of Unit 4: the present continuous (positive, negative, questions), weather words and -ing spelling. A weather report gives the place, the weather now and what people are doing. It often ends with advice (Take…, Wear…). Here are some examples. It's raining heavily in Abha. People are carrying umbrellas. It isn't snowing in Riyadh. Be careful! Some learners say: “In Tabuk is snowing.” That’s not right. We say: “In Tabuk, it is snowing.” English needs a subject: it. Quick check: what is wrong with “People is walking by the sea.”? … Think! … It should be “People are walking by the sea.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present a weather report.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Listen! The baby ___.","options":["is crying","are crying","crying","cries"],"answer":"is crying","explanation":"Now / Look! / Listen! → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"now وLook! تدل على المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"I ___ a warm scarf.","options":["wearing","are wearing","am wearing","is wearing"],"answer":"am wearing","explanation":"I → am + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"I مع am والفعل مع ing."},{"q":"The farmers ___ in the rain.","options":["working","works now","is working","are working"],"answer":"are working","explanation":"you / we / they → are + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"you وwe وthey مع are."},{"q":"","options":["My uncle are driving in the fog.","My uncle is drive in the fog.","My uncle driving in the fog.","My uncle is driving in the fog."],"answer":"My uncle is driving in the fog.","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing للفعل."},{"q":"It ___ today. The sky is blue.","options":["doesn't raining","isn't raining","not raining","aren't raining"],"answer":"isn't raining","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"___ your cousins visiting you?","options":["Does","Are","Do","Is"],"answer":"Are","explanation":"Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال يبدأ بـ am أو is أو are."},{"q":"What ___ Grandma cooking?","options":["do","does","are","is"],"answer":"is","explanation":"What/Where + am/is/are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"What ثم are ثم الفاعل."},{"q":"Is the wind blowing? – Yes, it ___.","options":["blows","is","are","does"],"answer":"is","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, it is. / No, they aren't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة."},{"q":"","options":["Is you listening to the radio?","Are you listening to the radio?","Do you listening to the radio?","You are listening to the radio?"],"answer":"Are you listening to the radio?","explanation":"Don't use do with the present continuous.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم do مع المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["We isn't going to the park today.","We not going to the park today.","We aren't going to the park today.","We don't going to the park today."],"answer":"We aren't going to the park today.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"There is a lot of rain. It's ___.","options":["rain","rainly","rains","rainy"],"answer":"rainy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"The sun is out. It's a ___ day.","options":["sunny","sunly","suny","sun"],"answer":"sunny","explanation":"Short vowel + one consonant → double it (sunny, foggy).","explanation_ar":"ضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"It's 5°C. Wear a ___.","options":["jacket","pair of sandals","swimsuit","sun hat"],"answer":"jacket","explanation":"wear clothes; carry/take an umbrella.","explanation_ar":"نرتدي الملابس ونحمل المظلة."},{"q":"Which is the coldest?","options":["hot","warm","freezing","cool"],"answer":"freezing","explanation":"freezing → cold → cool → warm → hot.","explanation_ar":"سلم درجات الحرارة."},{"q":"The storm is loud. It's a ___ night.","options":["stormly","stormes","stormy","stormmy"],"answer":"stormy","explanation":"noun + -y = weather adjective (rain → rainy).","explanation_ar":"الاسم + y = صفة الطقس."},{"q":"","options":["Take you umbrella. It's rainy.","Take your umbrella. It's rainy.","Wear your umbrella. It's rainy.","Take your umbrella. It's rain."],"answer":"Take your umbrella. It's rainy.","explanation":"wear clothes; carry/take an umbrella.","explanation_ar":"نرتدي الملابس ونحمل المظلة."},{"q":"hope → ___","options":["hopeing","hopping","hopng","hoping"],"answer":"hoping","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"dig → ___","options":["diging","diggging","digging","digeing"],"answer":"digging","explanation":"Short vowel + one consonant → double it (sunny, foggy).","explanation_ar":"ضاعف الحرف الأخير."},{"q":"die → ___","options":["diing","dyeing","dying","dieing"],"answer":"dying","explanation":"ie → y + ing.","explanation_ar":"ie تتحول إلى y."},{"q":"","options":["It is snowwing on the mountain.","It is snoweing on the mountain.","It is snoing on the mountain.","It is snowing on the mountain."],"answer":"It is snowing on the mountain.","explanation":"Two vowels or w/x/y at the end → don't double.","explanation_ar":"لا نضاعف بعد حرفين متحركين."},{"q":"","options":["The girls are skating on the ice.","The girls are skatting on the ice.","The girls is skating on the ice.","The girls are skateing on the ice."],"answer":"The girls are skating on the ice.","explanation":"Silent e → drop it, then add -ing.","explanation_ar":"نحذف e الصامتة."},{"q":"Which sentence is best for the TV weather news?","options":["In Dammam, it windy and the boats don't sailing.","In Dammam, it's windy and the boats aren't sailing.","In dammam, it's wind and the boats aren't sailing.","In Dammam, is windy and the boats not sailing."],"answer":"In Dammam, it's windy and the boats aren't sailing.","explanation":"Negative: am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ isn't وaren't."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"in abha is raining.\"","options":["In Abha, it is raining.","In abha, it is raining.","In Abha, it raining.","In Abha is raining."],"answer":"In Abha, it is raining.","explanation":"Weather sentences need it: It's raining.","explanation_ar":"جمل الطقس تحتاج it."},{"q":"What are you doing? – ___","options":["I'm reading about storms.","I'm read about storms.","I read about storms now.","I reading about storms."],"answer":"I'm reading about storms.","explanation":"What/Where + am/is/are + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"What ثم are ثم الفاعل."}],"theme_ar":"الطقس والفصول","essential_question_ar":"كيف يغيّر الطقس ما نفعله؟","can_do":"I can describe the weather and say what people are doing now with the present continuous.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف الطقس وأقول ماذا يفعل الناس الآن باستخدام المضارع المستمر."});
